{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "TypR Introduction",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# TypR — Typed R\n\nTypR is a typed superset of R that compiles to standard R code.\nIt adds type annotations, type checking, and generics while\nkeeping full R compatibility.\n\n**Syntax notes:**\n- Statements end with semicolons: `let x <- 42;`\n- Function bodies require braces: `function(x) { x * x }`\n- TypR doesn't support variadic functions yet, so `cat(\"x =\", x)` won't work. Use `cat(paste(\"x =\", x));` instead.\n- Prefer `cat()` over `print()` — `print()` may duplicate output due to webR auto-print.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let x <- 42;\n# Variadic cat not yet supported — use paste() to combine args\ncat(paste(\"x =\", x));",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "basics"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "# Function bodies require braces\nlet add <- function(a, b) { a + b };\nlet result <- add(3, 4);\n# Use cat() not print() to avoid duplicate output (webR auto-print)\ncat(result);",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "functions"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "let greeting: char <- \"Hello from TypR!\";\n# Use cat() not print() to avoid duplicate output\ncat(greeting);",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "typed"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "# Function bodies require braces\nlet square <- function(x) { x * x };\nlet result <- square(7);\n# Variadic cat not yet supported — see cell [1]\ncat(paste(\"7 squared =\", result));",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "square"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Directives\n\nUse `#!show-r` in a cell to toggle viewing the generated R code.\nUse `#!typecheck` followed by code to type-check without executing.\nUse `#!transpile` followed by code to see the transpiled R output.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "#!transpile\nlet fib <- function(n) {\n  if (n <= 1) { n }\n  else { fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2) }\n};\ncat(fib(10));",
        "language": "typr",
        "name": "transpile_demo"
      }
    ]
  }
}
